# Core Conventions

Full detail: root `AGENTS.md`. Non-trivial work uses `.cursor/agents/` + `.cursor/skills/`.

Default model is Grok 4.6 for every parent session and every subagent. Do not switch models.

## Stack

- Ruby 3.2.8 / Rails 8.1.2 / Tailwind only / Stimulus only / ViewComponent / Reform / dry-rb / RSpec
- UI/UX design: rely on the shadcn/ui plugin (`shadcn` skill + `plugin-shadcn-shadcn` MCP tools) for any design or component decision
- Thin models; business logic in plain Ruby services (`app/services/<domain>/`, `self.call(...) = new(...).call` → `Result`); validation in Reform contracts
- Trailblazer (`Trailblazer::Activity`) ONLY in the flowchart source-code generator and the code it generates — never for other business logic
- Prefer mature gems over hand-rolled protocol/crypto; wrap behind a thin app service
- No backward-compatibility shims — treat as a brand-new app

## Multi-tenancy

- Most models need `customer_id`
- Platform owner customer: `81721200` (owner role may cross tenants)
- Roles are only `owner`, `admin`, `member` (see AGENTS.md reserved-role rules)

## I18n (hard rule)

- No hard-coded user-facing strings. Both `en` and `zh-CN` required.
- Views/components: `t("...")`; non-controller Ruby: `I18n.t("...")`
- Stimulus: English `default:` Value + server-passed `data-*-value`; never literal UI text in JS

## Git

- Do not auto-commit; only commit when explicitly asked
